{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK78oq6xHE4hPVfBzjv2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed `django/contrib/auth/migrations/0011_update_proxy_permissions.py` so the migration no longer tries to create permissions that already exist. I haven't run any tests, so the fix is untested.\n\nThe failure happens when a proxy model's content type already has permissions, for example because the model was recreated as a proxy. The old update moved the concrete model's permissions onto the proxy's content type anyway and hit the unique constraint on `(content_type_id, codename)`. The query now leaves out any permission whose codename already exists under the target content type, in both the forward and reverse directions.\n\nA permission skipped this way stays on its old content type rather than being merged or deleted. That keeps the change small, but it means the stale duplicate is left in place."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1237,"cache_read_input_tokens":19340,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1237},"output_tokens":240,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25963105-b612-4be2-81cc-241d6a838fea","uuid":"1997ed21-9257-4e8c-8375-cd949fcff64f","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:55:31.280Z","request_id":"req_011ChK78ohf72VisJVNn6ptc"}
